    email: "peter_geng@stu.pku.edu.cn"
abstract: >-
  BurnOmicsDB is a curated, standardized, and gene-centered database that
  integrates human burn injury transcriptomic evidence across tissues,
  post-injury time points, wound stages, and clinical contexts. Version 1.0.0
  contains six GEO datasets, 22 predefined differential-expression contrasts,
  448,735 gene-contrast result records, reproducible analysis code, and a
  static alias-aware gene-search website.
